From: LuneOS <team@webos-ports.org>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 05:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pipeline: simple: support the Rockchip VICAP capture block

The simple pipeline handler matches on the media device's driver name, and
rockchip-cif is not in its table, so a camera behind the Rockchip Video Capture
unit is never enumerated even when the whole media graph is present and linked.

On a PineTab2 (rk3566, ov5648) every link is established and enabled:

    ov5648 2-0036        -> dw-mipi-csi2rx fdfb0000.csi   [ENABLED]
    dw-mipi-csi2rx       -> rkcif-mipi0                   [ENABLED]
    rkcif-mipi0          -> rkcif-mipi0-id0 (/dev/video1) [ENABLED]

yet "cam -l" lists no cameras at all, because no pipeline handler claims a
media device whose driver is rockchip-cif.

VICAP is a plain capture interface - it receives CSI-2 data and writes it to
memory, with no ISP of its own, so the sensor's Bayer frames reach userspace
unprocessed. Enable the Software ISP for it, as qcom-camss and j721e-csi2rx
already do, so the handler can deliver a usable format rather than raw only.

Note the rk356x MIPI CSI-2 D-PHY can run in a split 2+2 configuration, which
this does not address: the PineTab2 wires its rear sensor to lanes D0/D1 and
its front sensor to D2/D3, and only the first is reachable while the PHY is
driven in full mode.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff -ruN sp_a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp sp_b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -264,6 +264,7 @@
 	{ "mtk-seninf", { { "mtk-mdp", 3 } }, false },
 	{ "mxc-isi", {}, false },
 	{ "qcom-camss", {}, true },
+	{ "rockchip-cif", {}, true },
 	{ "sun6i-csi", {}, false },
 };
 
